<!--
    The Names variants: every system in the carousel has its name beneath its drawing,
    so the neighbors can be read as well. A carousel item shows an image or a text, never
    both, so the names are part of copies of the drawings (see tools/build-named-art.js).
    That is also why they don't follow the font size, and why custom collections, which
    can't be known in advance, get the folder without a name.

    The selected system has its name in the drawing too, where the large title goes. The
    veil, in the page color, hides it. It sits above the carousel, which paints the page,
    and below the room light of the atmosphere schemes, which would otherwise show its
    edges. With the soft transitions it fades with the text, so the name of the system
    that arrives grows with its drawing and gives way to the title. Its position and the
    size of the carousel items are in the aspect ratio files.

    The neighbors are brighter than in the other variants: at the opacity of those, the
    names can hardly be read. The tags of the shared drawings say what the names say, so
    only the few systems that have the same name in ES-DE keep theirs.
-->

<theme>
    <view name="system">
        <carousel name="systemCarousel">
            <staticImage>${namedArt}</staticImage>
            <defaultImage>${namedArtFallback}</defaultImage>
            <unfocusedItemOpacity>0.55</unfocusedItemOpacity>
        </carousel>

        <image name="selectedNameVeil">
            <path>${pixel}</path>
            <origin>0.5 0.5</origin>
            <color>${bgColor}</color>
            <zIndex>20.5</zIndex>
        </image>
    </view>
</theme>
